From c9cdd3fc40ef95f21aa90b2d257e47dfd32c8121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iamwrm <iamwrm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 12:09:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat(fork): add HERDR_ECHO_TIMING keystroke-echo
 latency probe

Env-gated client-side probe measuring input-to-frame echo latency for
remote attach diagnosis (i0002 W0). At most one probe outstanding; first
frame after a probed key input closes it. HERDR_ECHO_TIMING=1 prints one
p50/p95/min/max summary to stderr when the client exits;
HERDR_ECHO_TIMING=verbose additionally reports rolling stats every 25
samples while typing.

On Windows only key presses/repeats and pastes start probes (mouse moves
and focus events are filtered); on Unix any raw stdin chunk counts. No
wire-protocol change; zero overhead when the env var is unset.
